(FIL-05: a file handle's modified and accessed properties return Unix timestamps.
 Also covers: FIL-06.
 Asserted as a range rather than a value, because the generator cannot
 predict a wall-clock stamp; 1700000000 is 2023-11-14, comfortably in the past.
 Run from the vox-fuzz worktree root; the probe creates everything it
 needs under vf_scratch/files/ and touches nothing else.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-05.vox -o p && ./p
 actual output:
   modified is a plausible unix timestamp
   accessed is a plausible unix timestamp
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/files".
open a file for writing called seedfile at "vf_scratch/files/stamps.txt".
Write "when" to seedfile.
Close seedfile.
open a file for reading called src at "vf_scratch/files/stamps.txt".
a number called 'the modification time' is src's modified.
a number called 'the access time' is src's accessed.
If 'the modification time' is greater than 1700000000 then,
    print "modified is a plausible unix timestamp".
If 'the access time' is greater than 1700000000 then,
    print "accessed is a plausible unix timestamp".
Close src.
